window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>My head belongs in Heaven. My heart belongs in Hell.</p> <p>Running from demons isn’t exactly as Laney expected.</p> <p>After saving her Shadowbringer from his fate in Hell, Laney returns to a hot mess on Earth—and she’s at the center of it. With Adne seeking revenge, the Hunters out for blood, and the original Shadowbringer dangling Cas’ soul over both their heads, Laney soon realizes that she needs to take matters into her own hands.</p> <p>Thank God, there is Gladys, who still remembers how to perform a ritual needed, and Avery and Tyler, who fight their own little battle against wicked Luc.</p> <p>And then there’s the thing with her Shadowbringer boyfriend not remembering who he truly is.</p> <p>Laney thought it was difficult to go to Hell and back, but she never considered the ramifications of learning the truth.</p> <p><b><i>Tethered</i></b><b> is the fourth and final book in Angelina J. Steffort’s young-adult paranormal-romance series Breath of Fate.</b></p>"; 
